;
; A capture program used by the loopback tests to sample the I2S signals
; produced by the library under test.
;
; The library outputs BCLK on GP10, which must be jumpered to GP21 (see
; test/shared/loopback-tests.h). The program samples the configured IN
; pin once per BCLK cycle, on the rising edge:
;
;   1. wait for a rising edge of BCLK
;   2. sample the data pin
;   3. wait for the falling edge of BCLK
;
; The waits use the absolute GPIO number (not the IN-base-relative pin
; number), because each capture state machine configures a different IN
; base pin and only GP21 is wired to BCLK.
;
; With in-shift configured for right shift and a push threshold of 32
; (sm_config_set_in_shift(config, false, true, 32)), each pushed word
; contains 32 consecutive samples with the first sample in bit 31.
;
.program capture
    wait 1 gpio 21
    in pins, 1
    wait 0 gpio 21
